On Tue, 24 Feb 2004, Yashichi wrote:
> Based on the discussions that have occurred so far, I'd like to submit the
> following definition for a Can of Beans.
>
> Frequency: 1 in 12 (without changing spinach, this will yield an overall
> 1 in 4 vegan special rate for tins, up from 1 in 6)

This sounds good.  I know NHINRL, but the canned meat to canned vegies
ratio is a bit high.  Of course of the canned vegetables in real life,
beans are the least likely to be vegan.

> Normal (90%):
> + Confer 20-500 Nutrition, like any other tin
> + Message "You consume {type} string beans."
>   (Hard to make Szechuan and french fried work with any other type of bean)

You don't have to use tintxts for the names. There's got to be 15 types of
canned beans you can use: soy(nutritious), red, black, green, refried,
pinto, garbonzo, baked, navy, mung, lima, fava, kidney, cannellini, etc.

> If the consensus is that even at the base rarity of conferring the
> teleport intrinsic is too high (after all, one could always wish for
> blessed tins cf. spinach), then an alternate scheme could be:
>
> Blessed (5%):
> + Confer 500 Nutrition
> 50% chance of {
>   + Message "Holy frijoles, these must be jumping beans!"
>   + 3 in 10 chance of granting teleportitis
>   + if teleport not granted, 1 in 12 chance of teleport control
>   + if neither intrinsic granted, Message "They don't seem hard to catch."
>   + Message "You consume refried beans."
> } else
> + Message "You consume baked beans."

Still too hign.  You don't need wishing to make a tin blessed.
For corpse tins, the chance of a teleportitis tin is in the ballpark of
1%. Teleport control is way too high for this.  It should be 0%. There are
only two ways to get perm TC.  Eating tengu and eating =oTC. So there is a
chance for vegans to get it. They just have to jump through lots of hoops.
Putting it in a tin (even with a chance as low as 3%) seems is giving it
away.

